{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97ac614ee24a33a3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9009\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t## Review Summary\n10\t\n11\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n12\tRecommendation: accept\n13\t\n14\tTriage consistency check: `triage: below-threshold` with `epic_count: 1` — consistent; the\n15\tsingle-epic output is correct by design and Step 0 takes precedence over priority-split logic.\n16\tContract validator: OK (body sections present, canonical component name \"Dashboard\",\n17\tno Rule 11 or priority-inheritance rules applicable to this decomposition).\n18\t\n19\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n20\t\n21\tBoth HLRs (HLR-1, HLR-2, both P2) map to RHAISTRAT-9009-E001, and the decomposition\n22\tsummary carries a traceability matrix with full coverage. Priority inheritance is not\n23\tapplicable (single epic, no P0 work, no blocking edges). Priority collapse is not flagged:\n24\tthe strategy is triaged below-threshold, and the HLR-2 doc touch-ups are incidental\n25\tfollow-on work from the same string change, which the triage exception explicitly permits\n26\tbundling. Out-of-scope items (CRD renaming, broader localization review) are correctly\n27\texcluded and restated in the epic's scope.\n28\t\n29\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n30\t\n31\tSingle epic, no edges: frontmatter `dependencies: []` matches the summary DAG (isolated\n32\tnode) and there is nothing to trace for cycles, invalid edges, or serialization. Critical\n33\tpath length 1 is within the S-size heuristic (1-2). No konflux/license-validation/repo-\n34\tonboarding pairings exist, so rules 7/8/10 parallelism constraints are not applicable.\n35\tNo un-captured data/artifact dependencies — the doc touch-ups consume only the label\n36\tchange produced within the same epic.\n37\t\n38\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n39\t\n40\tOne component (Dashboard), one team (R